.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLAB-VM-DEBUG-BUNDLE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm klab-vm-debug-bundle
.Nd capture a lab test machine's ZFS and kernel state as a bundle and an OpenZFS issue ready to file
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar distro run-id
.Op Ar address
.Op Fl -deep
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
When a lab test run goes wrong,
.Nm
connects to the test machine
.Ql klab-test- Ns Ar distro
\(em at
.Ar address ,
or the one libvirt knows for it \(em and collects, each command under a
timeout and several at once, in under a minute:
the kernel, its command line, modules and DKMS state;
.Ql zfs version ,
pool status, events and history, every property of every dataset, a
15-second per-device I/O sample,
.Ql zdb -C
and
.Ql zdb -h ;
every ZFS module parameter and kstat; the kernel log and the last two
hours of the journal; every process, and the kernel stack of every task in
uninterruptible sleep; the disks' SMART data; the installed packages; and
the host's side of the test.
A section that fails is marked in its file and the rest goes on: a
partial bundle is more use than none.
.Pp
It writes the bundle as a tar archive and fills in an issue template for
the OpenZFS tracker with the kernel, ZFS version, counts and last test.
.Xr klab 8
runs it when a run ends with failures, and when its watchdog finds a
test's log has stopped growing, before killing the test.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -deep
Also a 30-second
.Xr perf 1
profile with folded stacks, and 30 seconds of ZFS tracepoints.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the header comment and exit 0.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /root/klab/ Ns Ar run-id Ns Pa / Ns Ar distro Ns Pa -debug-bundle.tar.gz
The bundle; its path is printed on standard output.
.It Pa /root/klab/ Ns Ar run-id Ns Pa / Ns Ar distro Ns Pa -ISSUE.md
The issue, ready to paste.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 when the bundle is written; 1 when the machine has no address, which
still writes a bundle saying so; 2 when
.Ar distro ,
.Ar run-id
or
.Ar address
is not usable.
.Sh EXAMPLES
On a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30, with this release's
.Nm
first on the path:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ klab-vm-debug-bundle debian ../../etc
klab-vm-debug-bundle: not a usable distro or run id: ../../etc
# (exited 2)
$ klab-vm-debug-bundle debian 20260930-0100 '1.2.3.4 -oProxyCommand=id'
klab-vm-debug-bundle: not an IP address: 1.2.3.4 -oProxyCommand=id
# (exited 2)
.Ed
.Pp
Collecting; not run for this page, as no test machine was up:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# klab-vm-debug-bundle debian <run-id> --deep
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr klab 8 ,
.Xr kzfs-test 8 ,
.Xr zdb 8 ,
.Xr zpool-events 8
.Sh HISTORY
On 2026-09-30, writing this page: a run with no failures put
.Dq 0
twice, on two lines, into the bundle's
.Pa meta.json ,
which then was not JSON; and the run id and address went unchecked into
paths and an ssh command line.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
It logs in to the test machine as root with the lab's fixed password and
does not check its host key; the lab's machines are built to be thrown
away.
